From 21620f6da031bfd948714c37f427809a700e6763 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: a card "3D: HDR" whose answer is kept for
 the display

Nothing that a display sends says whether it shows HDR in 3D: its EDID
says what it takes in 2D, and a projector that takes HDR10 refused the
3D mode of an HDR10 picture ("3D settings are not supported in HDR
video"). "How 3D video goes out" at Automatic sends SDR in 3D until
that is known for the display, and HDR where it is known that the
display shows it (Kodi, kodi-9473). The check gets a card that finds it
out, "3D: HDR", where a display connected says in its EDID that it
takes 3D and the 3D output of Hades is on:

- it plays the HDR 3D clip of hades-check (hades-check-3d-hdr10-sbs.mkv:
  the HDR10 card for each eye, half side by side, 1080p at 24000/1001,
  its Matroska StereoMode set) in the display's 3D layout, with the 3D
  settings that the frame packing card sets and "How 3D video goes out"
  at HDR, those that are not so already; the journal of the check has
  them, and every one is put back after (hades-check-restore puts them
  back before Kodi starts again if it stops in the middle);
- it reads what went out (hades.out.stereo, hades.out.stereo3d) and the
  key of the display (hades.out.displaykey: the make and model of its
  EDID, as Kodi keeps a display by);
- where HDR went out in 3D, it asks how the display showed it: in 3D
  and in HDR; in 3D, but pale, too dark or with wrong colours; as two
  pictures; no picture or a message. The first keeps "hdr" for that
  display, the others "sdr", in /storage/.kodi/userdata/hades-3d-hdr.txt,
  the file that Kodi reads as each 3D video starts: one line of
  key<TAB>value a display, the 32 used last, written whole and put in
  place. Another display's line is never changed. Where HDR did not go
  out in 3D, where no 3D went out, without an answer, or for a display
  that reports no make and model, nothing is kept, and the card says
  why;
- the summary of the check, which a diagnostic report carries, has one
  line of it.

"Everything" leaves the card out: it keeps an answer for the display,
which a quick check of everything should not do unasked.

Strings 33870 to 33879 and 33887 to 33889, in English, es_es, es_ar and
es_mx.
